      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ferran Park, opened in 1918, hosts the historic Alice McClelland Memorial Bandshell, a parabolic‑acoustic landmark built in 1926.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        3,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eustis%2C_Florida",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Clifford House, once a private residence, now houses the Eustis Historical Museum and Preservation Society.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.floridavisiting.com/list/eustis/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Eustis once sat on the Orange Belt Railway and later the Atlantic Coast Line, though those tracks are now dormant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eustis%2C_Florida",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Since 1902, Eustis has celebrated GeorgeFest, a Washington Birthday Celebration that still rings through the streets each year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.eustis.org/Residents/Live-Eustis/History",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Founded in 1884, Eustis grew around Lake Eustis, with its downtown stretching along the lakefront.",
